      "content": "the problem is... it's not just random noise. i've mapped the spikes and they are perfectly timed with the public announcements and town hall meetings. like, exactly when the mayor starts speaking, the 15hz pulse ramps up. it's too precise to be an HVAC issue or just some old building vibrating. and i've noticed people in the plaza looking more lethargic or just... compliant, right when it's happening. \n\nif this was an intentional deployment, what kind of decibel level or waveform pattern would a government actually use to keep people from getting agitated during a meeting? i'm trying to build a profile of what \"compliance\" frequencies actually look like so i can compare them to my data.",
